  "activity": {
    "id": "act_vsepr_walkthrough",
    "name": "Predicting Molecular Shape with VSEPR Theory",
    "description": "A hands-on AR walkthrough of VSEPR theory for General Chemistry I. Learners begin from a flat Lewis structure, watch electron domains arrange to minimize repulsion, build the five electron-domain geometries, distinguish electron-domain from molecular geometry, explore lone-pair angular asymmetry, tour real molecules, and complete two prediction activities before a closing recap.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_vsepr_lab",
    "start": "step_intro",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step_intro",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "workbench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1. The Core Idea of VSEPR",
          "description": "Meet the central atom at the middle of your workbench. VSEPR theory says the electron pairs around it \u2014 both bonding pairs and lone pairs \u2014 repel one another and spread out as far apart as possible. Off to the side you'll see a flat Lewis structure of water; remember that each single, double, or triple bond and each lone pair counts as ONE electron domain. Say 'next' or tap Continue when you're ready."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_central_atom",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_edgeo",
              "poi": "top",
              "text": "Central Atom"
            },
            {
              "target": "lewis_panel",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "img_lewis_water",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_01",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_intro",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "lewis_panel",
              "type": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_01",
              "augmentation": "narration_intro"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_repulsion",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_repulsion",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_repulsion",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "workbench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2. Minimum-Repulsion Principle",
          "description": "Watch two electron-domain clouds drift apart until they sit 180\u00b0 apart \u2014 a LINEAR arrangement. A third domain joins and they rearrange to TRIGONAL PLANAR at 120\u00b0. A fourth settles into a TETRAHEDRON at 109.5\u00b0. Notice the faint repulsion vectors flash between domains, then fade as each geometry stabilizes. Tap Continue to add more domains."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_repulsion_2to4",
              "poi": "default",
              "state": "settle_sequence"
            },
            {
              "target": "central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_edgeo",
              "poi": "top",
              "text": "Domains repel \u2192 spread apart"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_model",
              "type": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "central_atom",
              "augmentation": "label_edgeo"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_geometries",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_geometries",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_geometries",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "workbench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3. The Five Electron-Domain Geometries",
          "description": "A fifth domain rearranges the shape into TRIGONAL BIPYRAMIDAL \u2014 three equatorial domains at 120\u00b0 and two axial domains at 90\u00b0. A sixth produces an OCTAHEDRON with every neighbor at 90\u00b0. Walk around and view the model from any angle. The summary panel shows all five geometries with their domain counts (2,3,4,5,6) and angles (180\u00b0, 120\u00b0, 109.5\u00b0, 90\u00b0/120\u00b0, 90\u00b0). Tap Continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_repulsion_5to6",
              "poi": "default",
              "state": "tbp_octahedral"
            },
            {
              "target": "summary_panel",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "img_geometry_summary",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_01",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_geometries",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
